# 3. Internal Working

This is where advanced interviews begin.

Consider:

```java
Animal a = new Dog();
a.sound();
```

There are two different types involved:

```text
Reference type                  Object type
     ↓                              ↓
   Animal                          Dog
```

At compile time:

```text
Animal a
   ↓
Compiler checks:
"Does Animal have sound()?"
   ↓
YES
```

At runtime:

```text
Actual object = Dog
       ↓
Dog overrides sound()
       ↓
Dog.sound() executes
```

This is **dynamic method dispatch**.

### Important distinction

```text
Compile time
     ↓
Reference type determines
what members are accessible

Runtime
     ↓
Actual object determines
which overridden instance method executes
```

This distinction is extremely important in Java interviews.

