# 5. The Four Pillars — Advanced View

## 5.1 Encapsulation

Not simply:

> "Wrapping data and methods together."

Advanced interpretation:

> **Encapsulation controls access to an object's internal state and preserves its invariants by forcing state changes through controlled operations.**

Example:

```java
class BankAccount {

    private double balance;

    public void withdraw(double amount) {
        if (amount <= 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException();
        }

        if (amount > balance) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Insufficient balance");
        }

        balance -= amount;
    }
}
```

The important part is not `private`.

The important part is:

```text
External code
      ↓
Controlled API
      ↓
Validation
      ↓
State change
```

