# 7. Polymorphism

## Compile-time polymorphism

Method overloading:

```java
class Printer {

    void print(int value) {}

    void print(String value) {}

    void print(double value) {}
}
```

The compiler selects the method based on the argument list.

```text
print(10)
   ↓
print(int)

print("Java")
   ↓
print(String)
```

---

## Runtime polymorphism

Method overriding:

```java
class Payment {
    void pay() {
        System.out.println("Payment");
    }
}

class UPI extends Payment {
    @Override
    void pay() {
        System.out.println("UPI");
    }
}

Payment p = new UPI();
p.pay();
```

Output:

```text
UPI
```

