# 8. ⭐ Method Overloading vs Overriding

| Feature                       | Overloading         | Overriding      |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------- | --------------- |
| Polymorphism                  | Compile-time        | Runtime         |
| Same method name              | Yes                 | Yes             |
| Parameters                    | Must differ         | Must be same    |
| Inheritance required          | No                  | Yes             |
| Return type alone sufficient? | ❌ No                | ❌ No            |
| Binding                       | Static/compile-time | Dynamic/runtime |
| `static`                      | Can overload        | Cannot override |
| `final`                       | Can overload        | Cannot override |
| `private`                     | Can overload        | Cannot override |

### Interview trap

This is **not** overloading:

```java
int add(int a, int b)
double add(int a, int b)
```

Return type alone cannot distinguish overloaded methods.

