# 15. ⭐ Upcasting / Downcasting

### Upcasting

```java
Dog dog = new Dog();

Animal animal = dog;
```

Safe:

```text
Dog
 ↓
Animal
```

---

### Downcasting

```java
Animal animal = new Dog();

Dog dog = (Dog) animal;
```

Explicit.

Potential problem:

```java
Animal animal = new Cat();

Dog dog = (Dog) animal;
```

Runtime:

```text
ClassCastException
```

Use `instanceof` when appropriate:

```java
if (animal instanceof Dog dog) {
    dog.bark();
}
```

---

# 16. Covariant Return Type

Parent:

```java
class Animal {
    Animal create() {
        return new Animal();
    }
}
```

Child:

```java
class Dog extends Animal {

    @Override
    Dog create() {
        return new Dog();
    }
}
```

`Dog` is a subtype of `Animal`.

Therefore Java allows the more specific return type.

---

# 17. Constructor Chaining

```java
class Parent {

    Parent() {
        System.out.println("Parent");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {

    Child() {
        super();
        System.out.println("Child");
    }
}
```

Execution:

```text
new Child()
    ↓
Child constructor
    ↓
super()
    ↓
Parent constructor
    ↓
Child constructor body
```

### Important

Constructors:

* are not inherited
* cannot be overridden
* can be overloaded
* can call `this()`
* can call `super()`

