# 19. SOLID Connection

Advanced OOP eventually leads to SOLID.

```text
S → Single Responsibility
O → Open/Closed
L → Liskov Substitution
I → Interface Segregation
D → Dependency Inversion
```

### Most important OOP connection

**Liskov Substitution Principle**

If:

```text
Dog extends Animal
```

then code expecting an `Animal` should generally be able to work correctly with a `Dog` without breaking behavioral expectations.

This is much deeper than simply saying:

> "Child can replace parent."

