# 21. Bad Design vs Good Design

### ❌ Bad

```java
class OrderService {

    void pay(String type) {

        if (type.equals("UPI")) {
            // UPI logic
        }
        else if (type.equals("CARD")) {
            // Card logic
        }
        else if (type.equals("WALLET")) {
            // Wallet logic
        }
    }
}
```

Every new payment type modifies `OrderService`.

---

### ✅ Better

```java
interface PaymentStrategy {
    void pay();
}
```

```text
PaymentStrategy
      │
 ┌────┼────────┐
 ↓    ↓        ↓
UPI  Card    Wallet
```

Then:

```java
class OrderService {

    private final PaymentStrategy payment;

    OrderService(PaymentStrategy payment) {
        this.payment = payment;
    }

    void checkout() {
        payment.pay();
    }
}
```

Now:

```text
OrderService
     ↓
Interface
     ↓
Implementation
```

This gives:

* lower coupling
* easier testing
* easier extension
* polymorphism
* dependency inversion

