# 23. Common Candidate Mistakes

| Wrong Statement                        | Correct Understanding                                                 |
| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Static methods are overridden          | They are hidden                                                       |
| Private methods are overridden         | They are not inherited/overridden                                     |
| Return type can distinguish overloads  | Parameter list must differ                                            |
| Same hash code means objects are equal | Equal objects must have same hash code                                |
| `==` compares object content           | It compares references for objects                                    |
| Constructors are inherited             | They are not                                                          |
| Constructors can be overridden         | They cannot                                                           |
| Inheritance is always better for reuse | Composition is often preferable                                       |
| Interface has no implementation        | Modern Java interfaces can have default/static/private methods        |
| Runtime polymorphism applies to fields | Fields are resolved differently; field access is not virtual dispatch |

